<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">gore</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">gore</ansi> command launches a horned creature into a
charging strike that drives the target backward. It deals
solid damage and has a strong chance to knock the target
to the ground on a successful hit.

<ansi fg="yellow">Requirements:</ansi>

  - Must have a gore natural attack (horned species)
  - Must be in active combat
  - Cannot be used if special move cooldown is active

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">gore</ansi>
  Attempt to gore your current combat target

<ansi fg="yellow">Mechanics:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Damage:</ansi> Solid — the charging impact deals meaningful
    harm on contact.
  <ansi fg="stat">Knockdown:</ansi> A successful gore has a strong chance to
    drive the target backward off their feet (Supine),
    leaving them vulnerable to follow-up attacks.
  <ansi fg="stat">Cooldown:</ansi> Shared with other special moves.
  <ansi fg="stat">Skill:</ansi> Progresses Unarmed Combat

Gore is a powerful opener that combines direct damage with
a knockdown attempt. Unlike pounce, it relies on raw
strength and momentum rather than agility. See
<ansi fg="command">help conditions</ansi> for details on Supine.

